From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:49:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/39] nxhost input: virtual motion sensor, mouse aiming, full
 keyboard layout

The keyboard player now reports an emulated six-axis sensor unless a real
controller supplies motion (NX_KEY_GYRO=0 turns it off). Mouse movement
while captured (M in the game window, Esc or focus loss releases) and the
I/K keys turn it; the turn is spread over ~12 ms so games reading one
sample per frame still see all of it. Gravity follows the virtual pitch.
Axis signs checked in Splatoon 3: +x aims down, +z turns left.

Captured mouse buttons: left ZR, right R, middle right-stick click. New
keys: Space B, left Shift ZL, F right-stick click, G left-stick click.
NX_AUTOINPUT gains AIMUP/AIMDOWN/AIMLEFT/AIMRIGHT. Tunables:
NX_MOUSE_SENS (rad per point, 0.003), NX_KEY_GYRO_RATE (rad/s, 1.5).
